findings.comment:
750.800b - The following food contact surfaces were soiled:
A) can opener blade (food debris) - taken to dish area during inspection to go through ware washing;
B) top inside cook line microwave (food splash);
C) pan in a box of food in walkin freezer (food debris);
D) knives on both ends of cook line (food debris & stored on soiled shelving used to house coolers and microwaves);  and
E) around edges of pans in grill coolers (food debris)

Clean and sanitize food contact surfaces between uses/as needed, up to every 4hrs after continuous use, to prevent cross contamination and eliminate buildup of debris.

750.800e - The following non-food contact surfaces were soiled:
A) under crock storage and soup/chili hot holding - across from salad cooler (food debris/dust);
B) bottom inside all freezers - both ends of the cookline (food debris & ice buildup);
C) shelving of above counter coolers and microwaves - on cookline (dust/food debris); 
D) flat grills - legs and underneath surfaces (food debris/grease);
E) trays used for storage throughout (food/general debris);
F) 4 door cooler on server line - tracks and door seals (mold/debris);
G) weekend breading station (food splash); 
H) around door seals of dish machine (buildup); 
I) fryers - inside lower compartments (grease/food debris);  and
J) unused mop bucket in chemical storage room (moisture/glitter).

Clean non-food contact surfaces daily/as needed to eliminated buildup of debris.

findings.citation_text:
750.1200 & 1220 - A) Floor tile in front of fryer was damaged and observed to be holding moisture and debris. Repair the floor tile.

B) Floors were soiled in the following areas:
1. dish area - under the dish machine and alone the walls/in corners (grimy buildup);
2. under/behind ice machines (moisture/debris);
3. server line - corner under counter at north end (debris);
4. under shelving in walkin freezer;  
5. cook line - under all equipment on both sides (grease/food/general debris);  and
6. chemical storage room - under shelving (debris).
Clean the floors throughout daily/as needed to eliminate buildup of debris.

All floors must be in good repair, constructed to facilitate easy cleaning, and maintained clean.

750.1220 - Walls were observed to be soiled with splash/general buildup throughout the facility, including but not limited to:
1. around ice machines;
2. in dish area;
3. at mopsink; 
4. on cook line;   and
5. on server line below counters.

Clean the walls throughout daily/as needed, and maintain them clean.

